      "writtenOn": "2026-09-23T07:57:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately this doesn\u0027t really address my concern. My concern was actually answered by you in your reply, why would we ever not be supplying the refs? To address that, I would expect the method name to be something like getUrlForDelete() and getUrlForReplication(). Generality in Java we need not include parameter names in the method name because the type usually conveys that info (but not always such as when it is ambiguous, and the Strings are almost always ambiguous), so we often use the returned value to differentiate things. In this case, that might be something like getAllUrls(), and gerUrl(). \n\nBut I don\u0027t think we can make things that simple, because the purpose of this class is policy, so I think the method names do need to know the reason for the request in order to keep the policy decisions inside this class, and not in the rest of the plugin. I suspect that means we cannot use the same method for deletion and full Sync. Afterall, the policy needs to be different for these, and that policy needs to change with the strategy. In the case of deletions, some strategies should only delete from one url, and others should delete from all. That policy should not be the same for a full Sync, if it is, I think it is buggy?!\n\nMaybe the following would work? urlsToDeleteFrom(), urlsToReplicateTo() which would understand \"..all..\"?",
      "parentUuid": "aa2b05b9_dfa220d3",
      "revId": "6961c8d41816e28f3437788b0bc497c5ff0fb10f",
